they have very meaningful lives report more anxiety, more struggle, more difficulty, more stress, they didn't have more children. They might be happy, but they're struggling. Well, there are people who claim to have very happy lives whose lives contain comparative relatively less struggle and difficulty. Your book also talks about the connection between suffering and morality, the idea that if you do something that in any way benefits yourself, people won't see it as altruistic or good. So where does this idea come from that doing good has to somehow hurt, has to be painful?

